==French==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|frm|tous}} < {{inh|fr|fro|toz}}. {{surf|fr|tout|-s}}.

===Pronunciation===
* Pronoun and adjective in liaison:
** {{fr-IPA|tous‿}}
* Pronoun otherwise:
** {{fr-IPA|touç}}
** {{audio|fr|Fr-tous.ogg|audio}}
** {{a|Quebec}} {{IPA|fr|/tʊs/}}
* Adjective otherwise:
** {{fr-IPA}}
** {{audio|fr|Fr-tout.ogg|audio}}

===Pronoun===
{{fr-pron|m-p}}

# [[all]]
#: {{uxi|fr|Ils étaient '''tous''' là.|They were '''all''' there.}}
# [[everybody]]
#: {{uxi|fr|'''Tous''' étaient là.|'''Everybody''' was there.}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|fr|tout}}

===Adjective===
{{head|fr|adjective form}}

# {{masculine plural of|fr|tout}}
#: {{uxi|fr|Je me brosse les dents '''tous''' les jours.|I brush my teeth '''every''' day.|lit=I brush my teeth '''all''' the days.}}

====Usage notes====
To distinguish between the pronoun and adjective pronunciations, the adjective /tu/ is used before a noun (tous les jours) while the pronoun /tus/ occurs in isolation (Ils sont tous venus.)

====Related terms====
* {{l|fr|tout le monde}}

